  "gloss": "king; reign, kingdom; counsel",
  "summary": "מֶלֶךְ is a king, and מָלַךְ is to be or become king; the nouns name kingship, royal dignity, a reign, or the kingdom ruled. Scripture applies the family both to human rulers and to יַהְוֶה’s rule. The spelling also holds counsel-language, clear in Aramaic מְלֵךְ and Syriac verbs for advising and promising; its relation to kingship is not established by the cited uses.",
